.TH COREGLOW 1 "2026-11-01" "coreglow 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coreglow, coreglow-tray \- window and tray icon for Coreglow lighting and fans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coreglow
.RB [ \-\-page " " home | lighting | fans | profiles ]
.br
.B coreglow-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coreglow
is the window ("Coreglow" in the application menu). Its pages:
.TP
.B Home
Live temperatures with 10-minute graphs, fan and pump speeds, a picture of
the PC (click a part to change its lighting) and quick changes.
.TP
.B Lighting
The effect for the whole PC, or for a single part, with colour presets,
recent colours and live previews. Motherboard sync through OpenRGB is
switched on here.
.TP
.B Fans
Fan curve or fixed speed, presets, a test button, and the backup curve the
controller uses when Coreglow isn't running.
.TP
.B Profiles
Profiles, and the rules that switch them automatically (temperature,
running program, time of day, locked screen).
.PP
Changes are saved and applied as you make them.
.PP
.B coreglow-tray
shows an icon in the system tray (StatusNotifierItem) with the profile list,
automatic switching on/off, test fans and a way to open the window. It starts
at login.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COREGLOW_LANG
.B en
or
.B sk
overrides the interface language (otherwise taken from LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES or LANG).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coreglowd (1),
.BR coreglowctl (1)
